# Montreal (pop 7). Fixture: stock tools 100, muskets 100, horses 100; Church added.
# People strip icons: x = 5 + 9*i, y = 155. Dropping a colonist on the empty left edge of the fence strip
# opens the "leave as" popup (rows y: Colonist 46, Pioneer 54, Soldier 62, Scout 70, Dragoon 78, Missionary 86).
# Rows whose gear is missing are greyed. Colonists leave from the end of the strip so indices stay put.
click 135 175              # open Montreal
wait 10
drag 59 155 131 112        # colonist 6 -> fence: role popup
click 100 46               # plain Colonist
drag 50 155 131 112        # colonist 5 -> fence
click 100 62               # Soldier (-50 muskets)
drag 41 155 131 112        # colonist 4 -> fence
click 100 54               # Pioneer (-100 tools)
drag 32 155 131 112        # colonist 3 (fisherman expert) -> fence
click 100 70               # Scout (-50 horses)
drag 23 155 131 112        # colonist 2 -> fence
click 100 78               # Dragoon (-50 muskets, -50 horses): all gear is used up now
drag 14 155 131 112        # colonist 1 (expert farmer) -> fence: every gear row is greyed
click 100 62               # greyed Soldier row: ignored, popup stays open
click 100 86               # Missionary (Church built, costs no cargo): leaves, keeps his Farmer specialty
drag 5 155 131 112         # last colonist 0 -> fence: popup
click 100 46               # Colonist: the last colonist would abandon the colony, confirm prompt
key Return                 # default answer "Never! That would be folly.": colonist 0 stays
key Escape                 # close the role popup
key Escape                 # leave Montreal
